    "explanationEn": "Part (c) is where a strong answer separates from the textbook one. Most answers stop at \"supply falls\", but the decline in quality matters as much and is theoretically more interesting: once price is controlled, the parties find other dimensions to adjust — quality, side conditions, even queuing time become a disguised price. Writing that \"adjustment shifts to dimensions other than price\" shows an understanding of what price control actually does. Part (d) asks for comment on an argument pushed to an extreme; identify the logical error first (a cap creates no units), then the distributional consequence (winners and those excluded), then a policy that works in the right direction. \"Disagree, the shortage worsens\" is half an answer.",
    "markingScheme": "（a）3 分 —— 指出 9 000 元為有效上限（1）；需求量上升、供應量下跌（1）；短缺為兩者在該價格下的差距，並說明其成因為價格不能上升（1）。\n（b）2 分 —— 兩種非價格分配方式各 1 分。\n（c）2 分 —— 供應數量下降並說明業主的反應（1）；質素下降並說明其機制（1）。只寫「供應減少」而無質素一項，此項最多 1 分。\n（d）2 分 —— 指出上限不會增加供應、短缺反而擴大（1）；指出成功租到者與被排除者處境不同，並提出方向正確的替代做法（1）。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案只列必達步驟與判準，刻意不提供可直接抄錄的完整答卷。交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
